eation events are recorded even if one logging call fails or the service is called from different entry points. This helps track SSO adoption patterns, identify which users are setting up authentication providers, and monitor the growth of Form Authentication usage across the platform.\n\nSuccessful SSO journey by formId (who/when/what)\n```sumologic\n_sourceCategory=formstack/prod/*\n(\"form_render\" or \"form_view\" or \"sso_authentication\" or \"saml_authentication\" or \"auth_successful\")\n| json auto\n| where formId=_FORM_ID_\n| sort by _messageTime asc\n| fields _messageTime, message, formId, accountId, authProviderId, userId, redirectUrlPath\n```\n\nThis query traces the complete user authentication journey for a specific form, from initial form access through successful SSO completion. It uses multiple event types that represent different stages: form_render/form_view for initial form loading, sso_authentication/saml_authentication for the authentication flow, and auth_successful for completion. Sorting chronologically and including key identifiers helps reconstruct exactly what happened during a user's SSO session, making it invaluable for debugging authentication issues or understanding the user experience.\n\nConfirm ACS/finalize success events for the form (tie to user/authProvider)\n```sumologic\n_sourceCategory=formstack/prod/*\n(\"sso_auth\" or \"saml_authentication\" or \"auth_successful\")\n| json auto\n| where formId=_FORM_ID_\n| sort by _messageTime asc\n| fields _messageTime, message, formId, accountId, authProviderId, userId, ip\n```\n\nThis query focuses specifically on the Assertion Consumer Service (ACS) endpoint and authentication finalization events for a form. It narrows the scope to just the SSO/SAML authentication and success events, filtering out form rendering events. This is useful for confirming that users are successfully completing the SSO/SAML response processing and being authenticated, and for tying specific authentication even